#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Hold the evidence contracts to the rule that evidence never gates an action.

Evidence attests an action's licence after the action and never supplies it,
so no evidence, delivery, registration or disposition state may gate, delay,
block, suppress or mark unavailable an approved Tier C action or any Tier D
execution. That rule is stated in several contracts, and a reversing edit to
any one of them has been able to pass every other checker. This one:

- requires each clause in CLAUSES, word for word, inside the section it names;
- scans every sentence of the evidence contracts for one that pairs a gating
  verb with an action (Tier C, Tier D, an approved, safety or runtime action),
  and refuses every such sentence that is not one of those clauses, so a new or
  reworded sentence of that shape fails until a reviewer adds it here.

Nothing here is regenerated from the text: the clause list is the allowlist.

    python3 scripts/check-evidence-patf-clauses
    python3 scripts/check-evidence-patf-clauses --mutations
    python3 scripts/check-evidence-patf-clauses --print-units

`--mutations` deletes each clause, reverses each clause's negation, appends a
reversed sentence to each contract, and re-pins: rebuilds the allowlist from
reversed text, as a mechanical regeneration would, and requires every mutant
to be refused. `--print-units` prints the sentences the scan matches.
"""

